Chalk this one up to the "stupid human tricks" book.  I forgot to
'make install' after rebuilding each time.

So, the things *I* changed for my site are as follows:

In src/Makefile:

CC = xlc
CFLAGS = -DPOSIX_TYPES -D_POSIX_SOURCE -D_XOPEN_SOURCE -O -I../include -c -qchars=unsigned

WINTTYLIB = -lcurses

In util/Makefile:

CC = xlc
CFLAGS = -DPOSIX_TYPES -D_POSIX_SOURCE -D_XOPEN_SOURCE -O -I../include -c -qchars=unsigned

In util/Makefile:
In include/config.h:

/* Section 1 */
#define TERMINFO

/* Section 3 */
typedef short int schar;
typedef unsigned short int uchar;

#define VISION_TABLES
/* #define BRACES */

In include/unixconf.h:

#define SYSV
/* #define SUNOS4 */
#define AIX_31

******************************

I'm sure I missed a few things so don't depend on this solely if you're
planning on compiling 3.1.3 for your RS/6000 .  And DON'T FORGET TO
'make install' AFTER COMPILING!!!

